 "sessions": [
  {
   "id": "A",
   "title": "Six plural tips + umlaut",
   "said": [
    "n.stadt",
    "n.hand",
    "d18.p.zwei_haende",
    "d18.p.wie_viele_tische",
    "d18.p.viele_buecher"
   ],
   "steps": [
    {
     "type": "video",
     "title": "Video: plural rules",
     "videoId": "3Aqc5WDKO9A",
     "channel": "YourGermanTeacher (Luzi)",
     "start": 63,
     "end": 562,
     "note": "Chapters: 1:03 nouns ending in -e · 2:16 masculine + e · 2:51 feminine + (e)n · 3:24 neuter + er · 4:03 no change · 5:05 foreign words + s · 6:07 summary · 7:21 bonus: umlaut · 8:48 practice.\n\nThe example words are on screen — pause to read them."
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "title": "The six tips",
     "skipFirst": true,
     "intro": "With these tips you get about 80 % of plurals right. The plural article is always **die**.",
     "cols": [
      "",
      "rule",
      "example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "1",
       "ends in -e → + n",
       "die Tasche → die Taschen"
      ],
      [
       "2",
       "der-word → + e",
       "der Tisch → die Tische"
      ],
      [
       "3",
       "die-word → + (e)n",
       "die Tür → die Türen"
      ],
      [
       "4",
       "das-word → + er",
       "das Bild → die Bilder"
      ],
      [
       "5",
       "der/das-words in -er, -en, -el; all -chen, -lein → no change",
       "das Messer → die Messer"
      ],
      [
       "6",
       "foreign words, ending in a vowel (-o, -a, -i, -y) → + s",
       "das Sofa → die Sofas"
      ]
     ],
     "note": "Not sure? Add **-e** — it's the most common plural ending. And from now on, learn every new noun **with its plural**. (die-words in -er / -el add -n: {de:die Schwester → die Schwestern}.)"
    },
    {
     "type": "phrases",
     "title": "Examples",
     "items": [
      "n.tasche",
      "n.lampe",
      "n.tisch",
      "n.stift",
      "n.tuer",
      "n.bild",
      "n.ei",
      "n.messer",
      "n.broetchen",
      "n.sofa",
      "n.buero",
      "n.handy"
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "title": "Bonus: the umlaut",
     "md": "Many plurals also get an umlaut (ä, ö, ü):\n\n- with **-e**: {de:die Stadt → die Städte}, {de:der Knopf → die Knöpfe}, {de:der Ball → die Bälle}\n- with **-er**: {de:das Haus → die Häuser}, {de:der Mann → die Männer}, {de:das Bad → die Bäder}\n- with **no ending**: {de:der Vater → die Väter}, {de:die Mutter → die Mütter}, {de:der Vogel → die Vögel}\n\n*a* → *ä*, *o* → *ö*, *u* → *ü*, *au* → *äu*."
    },
    {
     "type": "phrases",
     "title": "Plurals with umlaut",
